## Known, deliberately deferred gap

**Private subnet instance still cannot reach SSM** — by design, it has no internet route, so its (now correctly installed) SSM Agent has no path to Systems Manager's endpoints. The fix requires three Interface VPC Endpoints (`ssm`, `ssmmessages`, `ec2messages`) associated with the private subnet, using AWS's private network path instead of the internet. Not yet implemented — planned for the next session, along with a genuine design question still to resolve: whether the endpoints should share the existing instance security group or use a dedicated one, given they need to *accept* inbound HTTPS rather than only send outbound traffic.

